                <pb facs="1438" n="1428" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6463/5–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-05">May 5, 1945</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 5—10:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. For Clayton. Soong has not raised with me the question of assistance in
                    connection with the Yangtze Power Project referred to in your No. 31, May 4. He
                    has said, however, that he will raise all the economic matters in which he is
                    interested when he is in Washington next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
